<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Yehuling</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1211</span> · Also known as Battle of Badger Mouth · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-conquest-of-the-jin-dynasty">Mongol conquest of the Jin dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Yehuling, or Badger Mouth, was fought in 1211 at a mountain pass north-west of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhangjiakou">Zhangjiakou</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>'s first invasion of the Jin dynasty. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroyed a much larger Jin army, killing a great part of it and opening the way to the plains of northern China. It began more than twenty years of war that ended with the fall of the Jin in 1234.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-yehuling.jpg" alt="Battle of Yehuling" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sayf al-Vâhidî. Hérât. Afghanistan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_entre_mongols_%26_chinois_(1211).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
